<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muwatalli II</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muwatalli II was a king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-empire">Hittite Empire</a> in the early thirteenth century BCE. He commanded the Hittite forces against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramesses-ii">Ramesses II</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kadesh">Battle of Kadesh</a> in 1274 BCE, one of the largest <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chariot">chariot</a> battles of the ancient world. The battle ended without a decisive victory and is a key event in the military history of the Egyptian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a>.</p></div>
